+    obstacle (absent in L1/L2): actions 1/2 move the color-6 patterned
+    actuator vertically, actions 3/4 extend/retract its horizontal body;
+    the anchored column resists the same pull/lift/merge/row-reversal
+    constructions that solved L1/L2. Direct ACTION6 clicks and ACTION5 on
+    both glyphs produced no visible selection/release effect at any tested
+    coordinate -- reconfirms round 1''s finding that the glyph does not
+    respond to direct interaction. Stopped with 35 steps unspent, choosing
+    to preserve budget for the reproduction gate (passed for level 2)
+    rather than risk an unverified level-3 claim. No new level banked;
+    frontier stays at level 2.'
